A||||15||fropuff||Are paintjobs expensive?||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||04-13-2000||08:06 PM||||Hi, I just found a nice Fiero for sale here in Minnesota, it's a 1986 Fiero GT, automatic tranny, 65K miles, that's right.  Best of all, he gave me a great deal of $2200.  It was a California car, and the guy says it needs a new paint job.  Are they expensive?  Thanks||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||04-13-2000||08:12 PM||||depends on exactly what it needs and how you want to paint it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||04-13-2000||08:23 PM||||What I want is a paint job that looks professional.  Not one that is done in someone's crappy garage.  The paint is just a little faded, and I am wondering if it will look good with just a clear coat or an entire paint job.  Thanks.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-13-2000||08:43 PM||||I've seen some nice Macco paint jobs for $700.  I've seen nicer paint jobs for $2000.  Remember, you get what you pay for.  theogre is right.  Get some estimates from some good body shops in your area.  The amount of preparation that is needed to get the car ready for painting is(?)important.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Cooter||04-13-2000||09:21 PM||||My area is so flooded with shops, in order to compete I have to do a $2000 paint job for less than $900. It aint easy! We have lost money for the past two years, but it is such a great hobby I cant give it up. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TooLowFiero||04-13-2000||09:59 PM||||if you get it try a product called Liquid Glass..  you can get it at most autoparts stores.. its about 15.00 bucks.. if the paint is just faded use this product and buff it out.. will make the paint shiny again(did it to my car)and it looks great... just my $.02||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||04-14-2000||01:18 AM||||I got a $1700 quote for a complete repaint at a very reputable shop. This guy has done body work on many show cars and customs. He stands behind his work 100%. Although, I'd rather take a daily driver to Cooter and save some dough.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||04-14-2000||01:24 AM||||2Low has a good point- before you make the jump to a new paint job, take the time and a moderate amount of effort to bring your existing paint back I have yet to see a respray that I couldn't tell was a respray if examined close enough. <BR>I drive a gold Fiero- one of the more infamous colors for oxidizing and turning into a muddy haze.  But by wetsanding with 1500 grit, polishing with 3M cuttig compound and good Meguir's wax, I now have a very respectable 10 foot paint job. eventually I will repaint, but it doesn't have to be the high priority in putting together a nice ride.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Racer 1||04-14-2000||01:26 AM||||I painted most of my fiero parts myself. I did the hood,front end and rear decklid,t-tops side bars and both front side fenders for like $100.00 with clear coat and thinner. But the aircompressor costed me $400.00 and Low pressure high volume sprayer deal. I think my Fiero turned out ok for a garage painted deal. Around here its around $900-1200 . ||||reg||8
Z||000009||fiero_86_se||04-14-2000||01:34 AM||||it depends on where you go and who you have to do it.   I know I could do a good one for about $200||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phoenix||04-14-2000||08:06 AM||||fropuff - Where in Minnesota do you live? I live in ST.Bonifacius (west of lake Minnetonka). I've painted many of my own cars in the past and I am planning on painting my Coupe sometime in the next month. Email me and we can hook up by phone. I can give you some tips to get a good paint job for a reasonable price.<P>paul@phoenixhobbies.com||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||04-14-2000||09:49 AM||||I guess another option to save some money would be to sand and prep the car yourself, and then take it to someplace like Maaco and have them paint it.  The big problems with paint jobs from those places is that often they dont take the time to properly prep the car.  If it is sanded and ready to go, you probably could get a decent paint job for $200.  I imagine that the paint guys would be happy they didnt have to bother with prepping it and may take some extra care during the painting process.<P>Depending on the shop, this method might cause warranty concerns, but I think this is a good way to save some dinero if the shop doesnt mind you doing this.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||04-14-2000||12:01 PM||||Hey!  two more minnesota members!  you guys going to the MFF spring kick-off?  send me an email..  <A HREF="mailto:fieromike88@netzero.net">fieromike88@netzero.net</A> <P>Just to get back on topic... I need a paint job, too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000013||fropuff||04-16-2000||04:54 PM||||The sun damage is on the entire roof panels, the rear deck lid, and the front fascia. I think that's all that will need to be repainted.  What will that cost?  (Not a Maaco paint job.)  The hood, doors, lower panels, and ground effects are good.  By the way, I did buy the Fiero yesterday for $2200.  He was originally asking $3000.  Good deal for a little paint, I think.||||reg||10
Z||000014||fropuff||04-18-2000||02:59 PM||||Anyone know???||||reg||6
Z||000015||CUTTER||04-18-2000||05:43 PM||||If you want to save some money do it yourself. I just repainted my front facia, spoiler, and ground-effects and y0ou can barly tell that it was done my me. and it cost about $15.00 for the sand paper paint and clearcoat. Some people said they would pay 2-300 for what i did for 15.00 it as long as you tape everything good and make sure its almost perfect it will look good. That was even my first time really painting anything. if your gonna use spray paint use "truck & Van paint", it works well. no runs, spots or anything. can get it all wal-mart.<BR>  Shane, blue 87GT||||reg||1
